Modifications in this copy
--------------------------

CipherStash made these changes:

- references/concurrency.md is adapted from skills/golang-pro/references/
  concurrency.md and the core pattern example in skills/golang-pro/SKILL.md.
  Its examples now live as Go source in examples/concurrency/, with tests,
  and these defects are fixed:
  - the pipeline example waited for its whole timeout on success and then
    returned a timeout error; RunJobs returns as soon as the work is done;
  - pipeline, fan-out and fan-in stages ranged over their input and checked
    the context only when sending, so they leaked when the input was never
    closed; every stage now also selects on the context when receiving;
  - the worker pool's Submit and the semaphore's Acquire blocked with no
    context, and pool tasks had no way to be cancelled; they now take one;
  - the worker pool's Shutdown and the server's done channel panicked when
    closed twice, and Submit after Shutdown panicked; shutdown is now safe
    to repeat and Submit returns ErrPoolClosed;
  - the timeout example ran a call that ignored its context in a goroutine
    raced against time.After, and returned an unwrapped error; Fetch passes
    the context to the request instead;
  - the cache wrote to a nil map, and the sync.Once example dropped the
    load error; they use a constructor and sync.OnceValues;
  - the server example printed instead of returning errors;
  - the rate limiter example, which imported golang.org/x/time/rate, is
    replaced by prose, so the examples module needs only the standard
    library;
  - the loop-variable advice depends on the module's Go version.
- references/error-handling.md is new.
- SKILL.md is new: a rule list and an index of references. The upstream
  frontmatter metadata, persona line, workflow, output template and list of
  related skills are not carried over, and "no naked returns" is not treated
  as an error-handling rule.
- examples/ and tests/ are new.
